AB  - This work presents UQEF-Dynamic, an open-source Python tool for forward uncertainty quantification and sensitivity analysis of models with time-varying outputs, such as hydrological and environmental systems. Existing tools rarely handle high-dimensional, computationally expensive models with vectorial or functional outputs, nor do they fully exploit modern high-performance computing. UQEF-Dynamic addresses these gaps with a scalable, portable framework supporting sampling-based methods and non-intrusive Polynomial Chaos Expansion (PCE), extended with Karhunen–Loève (KL) surrogates to reduce output dimensionality, and enabling time-varying and generalized Sobol’ sensitivity indices. Alongside the software, this work provides a unified treatment of the underlying mathematical methods. We demonstrate the framework through two case studies: an analysis of the HBV-SASK hydrological model, to our knowledge the most comprehensive analysis of this model, and the construction of a KL–PCE surrogate for a 24-dimensional electrochemical battery model. Results show that UQEF-Dynamic delivers efficient analysis and deeper insight into model behavior under varying conditions.
