AB  - Accurate modeling of reference evapotranspiration (ET0) is critical for environmental management but is hindered by input uncertainties and data scarcity in emerging agricultural frontiers. We introduce EVAonline, a new open-source, scalable web platform providing robust ET0 estimation via multi-source data fusion. Built on a modular hexagonal architecture integrating six meteorological APIs, the software implements an adaptive Kalman filter constrained by 30-year climatological priors to harmonize disparate datasets. Validated in Brazil’s MATOPIBA region across 17 sites (186,286 observations), the framework achieved a Kling-Gupta Efficiency of 0.814. The fusion process significantly mitigated uncertainty, reducing Mean Absolute Error by 50% and systematic bias by 95% compared to individual products. By resolving hydroclimatic modeling challenges in data-scarce regions through software engineering, EVAonline delivers a scalable, open-source decision-support architecture designed for global deployment; its quantitative validation here is restricted to the MATOPIBA region against BR–DWGD, with broader multi-climate and forecast-horizon validation left for future work.
