AB  - The present study improves the forest growth dynamics in the SWAT-C model for data limited tropical regions through dynamic initiation of the canopy growth cycle using the climate driven triggers. The improvement in the model was achieved by two approaches: (i) improving the parameters of the model obtained from MODIS LAI (M2) and (ii) through modification of source code (M3). The performance of both the modified models and default model (M1) was similar (NSE, KGE >0.75) for streamflow simulation. However, the improved models performed well in simulating ET, when compared against MODIST ET, with M2 and M3 reporting 19% and 21% lower bias than M1 in forested sub-basins. Similarly, the simulations of sediment yield and carbon storage dynamics varied in the three models. The study demonstrates the implication of these variations in management of natural resources, emphasizing the need for improving the forest growth dynamics.
